1
00:04:08,275 --> 00:04:14,275
Planet of the Apes is a thriller, science fiction,
action film directed by Tim Burton.

2
00:08:16,551 --> 00:08:22,551
After a spectacular crash-landing on an uncharted planet, brash astronaut Leo Davidson finds
himself trapped in a savage world where talking apes dominate the human race.

3
00:12:24,827 --> 00:12:30,827
Desperate to find a way home, Leo must evade the invincible
gorilla army led by Ruthless General Thade.

4
00:16:33,103 --> 00:16:39,103
Captain Leo Davidson, played by Mark Wahlberg.

5
00:20:41,379 --> 00:20:47,379
Thade, played by Tim Roth.

6
00:24:49,655 --> 00:24:55,655
Ari, played by Helena Bonham Carter.

7
00:28:57,931 --> 00:29:03,931
Attar, played by Michael Clarke Duncan.

8
00:33:06,206 --> 00:33:12,206
Limbo, played by Paul Giamatti.

9
00:37:14,482 --> 00:37:20,482
Daena, played by Estella Warren.

10
00:41:22,758 --> 00:41:28,758
Planet of the Apes is a 2001 American science fiction action adventure film directed by Tim
Burton from a screenplay by William Broyles Jr., Lawrence Konner, and Mark Rosenthal.

11
00:45:31,034 --> 00:45:37,034
The sixth installment in the Planet of the Apes film series, it is loosely based on the 1963 novel
of the same name by Pierre Boulle and serves as a remake of the 1968 film version.

12
00:49:39,310 --> 00:49:45,310
The film stars Mark Wahlberg, Tim Roth, Helena Bonham Carter, Michael Clarke
Duncan, Kris Kristofferson, Estella Warren, and Paul Giamatti.

13
00:53:47,586 --> 00:53:53,586
It tells the story of astronaut Leo Davidson (Wahlberg)
crash-landing on a planet inhabited by intelligent apes.

14
00:57:55,862 --> 00:58:01,862
The apes treat humans as slaves, but with the help of an ape named Ari
(Bonham Carter), Leo starts a rebellion as he seeks to return.

15
01:02:04,137 --> 01:02:10,137
Development for a Planet of the Apes remake started
as far back as 1988 with Adam Rifkin.

16
01:06:12,413 --> 01:06:18,413
His project nearly reached the pre-production stage before being canceled.

17
01:10:20,689 --> 01:10:26,689
Terry Hayes's script, titled Return of the Apes, would have starred
Arnold Schwarzenegger, under the direction of Phillip Noyce.

18
01:14:28,965 --> 01:14:34,965
Oliver Stone, Don Murphy, and Jane Hamsher were set to produce.

19
01:18:37,241 --> 01:18:43,241
Creative differences ensued between Hayes and 20th Century Fox.

20
01:22:45,517 --> 01:22:51,517
Chris Columbus, Sam Hamm, James Cameron, Peter Jackson, and
the Hughes brothers later became involved.

21
01:26:53,793 --> 01:26:59,793
With Broyles Jr.'s script, Burton was hired as director, and
the film was put into active development.

22
01:31:02,068 --> 01:31:08,068
Konner and Rosenthal rewrote the script, and filming took
place from November 2000 to April 2001.

23
01:35:10,344 --> 01:35:16,344
Planet of the Apes was released in the United States
on July 27, 2001, by 20th Century Fox.

24
01:39:18,620 --> 01:39:24,620
The film received mixed reviews from critics, who criticized the screenplay and twist ending, but
praised Rick Baker's prosthetic makeup designs, visual aspects, and musical score.

25
01:43:26,896 --> 01:43:32,896
It grossed $362.2 million worldwide, becoming the
ninth-highest-grossing film of 2001.

26
01:47:35,172 --> 01:47:41,172
Despite its financial success, Fox chose to cancel the sequel and later
rebooted the film series in 2011 with Rise of the Planet of the Apes.

27
01:51:43,448 --> 01:51:49,448
The film explores themes of space marine, gorilla,
revolution, dystopia, space suit.

28
01:55:51,724 --> 01:55:57,724
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
